// A relation's answer as legend-engine's own PCT adapter reads the engine's JSON result (pct_relational.pure: parseJSON,
// then fromJSON into its RelationalTDSResult with nullReplacementInArray=TDSNull): the TDS builder's columns, and each
// row's values as json-simple types them (an integral number an Integer, any other number a Float of its double, a JSON
// null TDSNull). getTDSResultFromProtocol's steps write it as the TDS text stringToTDS reads (pct_adapter.pure,
// engineTDS). The adapter's Java builds it from the engine JSON the server writes (PureV1Writer); 2026-10-27, the result
// boundary program's stage 1, step 3.
Class meta::legend::lite::pct::EngineTDSResult
{
    columns: meta::legend::lite::pct::EngineTDSColumn[*];
    rows: meta::legend::lite::pct::EngineTDSRow[*];
}

Class meta::legend::lite::pct::EngineTDSColumn
{
    name: String[1];
    type: String[0..1];
}

Class meta::legend::lite::pct::EngineTDSRow
{
    values: Any[*];
}
